SSHD_CONFIG(5)          File Formats Manual          SSHD_CONFIG(5)

NAME
     sshd_config — OpenSSH SSH daemon configuration file

SYNOPSIS
     /etc/ssh/sshd_config

DESCRIPTION
     sshd_config is the configuration file for the sshd daemon.  It
     contains keyword-value pairs, one per line.  Lines starting with
     '#' and blank lines are interpreted as comments.

     The options understood by sshd include:

     Port         Specifies the port number that sshd listens on.
                  The default is 22.

     PermitRootLogin
                  Specifies whether root can log in.  The default is
                  'prohibit-password'.

     PasswordAuthentication
                  Specifies whether password authentication is allowed.
                  The default is 'yes'.

FILES
     /etc/ssh/sshd_config

SEE ALSO
     ssh(1), sshd(8), ssh_config(5)